{"surah": 100, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلْعَٰدِيَٰتِ ضَبْحًا ", "translation": "By the racers, panting,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلْعَٰدِيَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyِdَٰʿعْlٱَw", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ضَبْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْbَḍ", "root": "ضبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "فَٱلْمُورِيَٰتِ قَدْحًا ", "translation": "And the producers of sparks [when] striking[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلْمُورِيَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyِrwُmْlٱَf", "root": "وري"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَدْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْdَq", "root": "قدح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "فَٱلْمُغِيرَٰتِ صُبْحًا ", "translation": "And the chargers at dawn,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلْمُغِيرَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰryِغُmْlٱَf", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صُبْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْbُṣ", "root": "صبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "فَأَثَرْنَ بِهِۦ نَقْعًا ", "translation": "Stirring up thereby [clouds of] dust,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَثَرْنَ", "translit": "َnْrَhtَaʾَf", "root": "ثور"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَقْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْqَn", "root": "نقع"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "فَوَسَطْنَ بِهِۦ جَمْعًا ", "translation": "Arriving thereby in the center[1] collectively,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَوَسَطْنَ", "translit": "َnْṭَsَwَf", "root": "وسط"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَمْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْmَjg", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لِرَبِّهِۦ لَكَنُودٌ ", "translation": "Indeed mankind, to his Lord, is ungrateful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِرَبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَrِl", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكَنُودٌ", "translit": "ٌdwُnَkَl", "root": "كند"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَإِنَّهُۥ عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكَ لَشَهِيدٌ ", "translation": "And indeed, he is to that a witness.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَشَهِيدٌ", "translit": "ٌdyِhَhsَl", "root": "شهد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وَإِنَّهُۥ لِحُبِّ ٱلْخَيْرِ لَشَدِيدٌ ", "translation": "And indeed he is, in love of wealth, intense.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِحُبِّ", "translit": "ِّbُḥِl", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْخَيْرِ", "translit": "ِrْyَhkْlٱ", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَشَدِيدٌ", "translit": "ٌdyِdَhsَl", "root": "شدد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "أَفَلَا يَعْلَمُ إِذَا بُعْثِرَ مَا فِى ٱلْقُبُورِ ", "translation": "But does he not know that when the contents of the graves are scattered", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَلَا", "translit": "āَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بُعْثِرَ", "translit": "َrِhtْʿعُb", "root": "بعثر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْقُبُورِ", "translit": "ِrwُbُqْlٱ", "root": "قبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَحُصِّلَ مَا فِى ٱلصُّدُورِ ", "translation": "And that within the breasts is obtained,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَحُصِّلَ", "translit": "َlِّṣُḥَw", "root": "حصل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلصُّدُورِ", "translit": "ِrwُdُّṣlٱ", "root": "صدر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "إِنَّ رَبَّهُم بِهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ لَّخَبِيرٌۢ ", "translation": "Indeed, their Lord with them, that Day, is [fully] Aware.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّهُم", "translit": "mُhَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَّخَبِيرٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢryِbَhkَّl", "root": "خبر"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"10": [{"arabic": "الأمور وبعثرت القبور وحصل ما في الصدور وأوقفتم للتحصيل بين يدي الملك الجليل فطارت القلوب لإشفاقها من سالف الذنوب وهتكت عنكم الحجب والأستار وظهرت منكم العيوب والأسرار هنالك تجزى كل نفس بما كسبت إن الله عز وجل يقول ليجزى الذي أساءوا بما عملوا ويجزى الذي أحسنوا بالحسنى وقال تعالى {ووضع الكتاب فترى المجرمين مشفقين مما فيه} الآية جعلنا الله وإياكم عاملين بكتابة متبعين لأوليائه حتى يحلنا وإياكم دار المقامة من فضله إنه حميد مجيد وقال بعض الحكماء الأيام سهام والناس أغراض والدهر يرميك كل يوم", "english": "And indeed there has come the narration from him, from his Lord, Mighty and Glorious, that He said to Moses, peace be upon him: \"When you see the rich man approaching, say: 'A sin whose punishment has been hastened.' And when you see the poor man approaching, say: 'Welcome to the badge of the righteous.'\" And if you wish, you may follow the possessor of the Spirit and the Word, Jesus son of Mary, peace be upon him — for he used to say: \"My condiment is hunger, my badge is fear, my garment is wool, my warmth in winter is the rising places of the sun, my lamp is the moon, my mount is my two feet, and my food and my fruit is what the earth brings forth. I pass the night and I possess nothing, and I rise in the morning and I possess nothing — and there is no one upon the earth richer than I.\"", "book_title": "Condemnation of the World", "section_title_ar": "Section 737", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 737: On the Censure of This World and the Description of Its Perils", "section_index": 737, "anchors": "- Root: دنو (danuww)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"دنا فهو دانٍ\" — proximity, nearness; the world (al-dunyā) is so named because it is nearer and lower, deferred from the Hereafter.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الدنو: القرب بالذات، أو بالحكم\" — proximity by essence or by decree; used of place, time, and station. The \"nearer\" (al-adnā) is contrasted with the greater and the better.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical nearness. Metaphorical: the lower, contemptible station — \"أهل الدناءة هم أهل الشناءة\" (the people of baseness are the people of abhorrence).\n- Root: يوم (yawm)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"اليوم\" — a day; also any period of time.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"اليوم يعبر به عن وقت طلوع الشمس إلى غروبها. وقد يعبر به عن مدة من الزمان أي مدة كانت\" — the day is the time from sunrise to sunset, or any duration whatsoever. \"وذكرهم بأيام الله\" — the days of God are His mighty deeds and calamities upon the disbelievers.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the solar day. Metaphorical: \"أيام العرب\" — their battles and vicissitudes; \"أيام الله\" — His punitive visitations.\n- Root: وقد (waqada)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"وقدت النار تقد وقودا ووقدا\" — the fire blazed; al-wuqūd is the fuel.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"وقودها الناس والحجارة\" — the fuel of the Fire is men and stones; the one who kindles it for himself (istawqada) is he who seeks its light.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: kindling a fire. Metaphorical: \"قلب وقاد\" — a blazing, keen heart; \"وقد الحصى\" — the pebbles became scorching hot (i.e., the intensity of the sun's heat).\n- Root: ألك (alaka)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"المألكة: الرسالة، لأنها تؤلك في الفم\" — the message (risālah) is called ma'lakah because it is chewed/worked in the mouth.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الملائكة تقع على الواحد والجمع\" — angels (malā'ikah) are so named as bearers of messages; \"الله يصطفي من الملائكة رسلا\" {«الله يصطفي من الملائكة رسلا»} — God chooses messengers from the angels.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: chewing (as a horse chews its bit). Metaphorical: delivering a message — the angel is the one who delivers the divine communication.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — \"إنما\" restricts the predicate to the subject alone, negating it of all else. Applied in the sermon: \"إنما يتزين لي أوليائي بالذل والخوف\" — My friends adorn themselves for Me ONLY with humility, fear, and submission — restricting their adornment to these alone, excluding all worldly ornament.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Condemnation of the World'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 2177], [2, 2177, 3286]], "2": [[1, 250, 2146], [2, 2146, 3208]], "3": [[1, 250, 2111], [2, 2111, 3260]], "4": [[1, 250, 1593], [2, 1593, 2074], [3, 2074, 3417]], "5": [[1, 250, 1662], [2, 1662, 2093], [3, 2093, 3182]], "6": [[1, 350, 1442], [2, 1442, 3314], [3, 3314, 4705], [4, 4705, 6349]], "7": [[1, 350, 1872], [2, 1872, 3029], [3, 3029, 3975], [4, 3975, 5383]], "8": [[1, 350, 1727], [2, 1727, 2603], [3, 2603, 3719], [4, 3719, 5017]], "9": [[1, 350, 1210], [2, 1210, 2053], [3, 2053, 2752], [4, 2752, 3523], [5, 3523, 3989], [6, 3989, 4437], [7, 4437, 5513]], "10": [[1, 350, 1384], [2, 1384, 1842], [3, 1842, 2282], [4, 2282, 3528]], "11": [[1, 350, 1312], [2, 1312, 2538], [3, 2538, 3302], [4, 3302, 4989], [5, 4989, 6663]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 280, 2404], [2, 2404, 4030]], "2": [[1, 390, 2481], [2, 2481, 4110]], "3": [[1, 200, 2320], [2, 2320, 4140]], "4": [[1, 10, 1361], [2, 1361, 1845], [3, 1845, 4010]], "5": [[1, 200, 1856], [2, 1856, 2298], [3, 2298, 4140]], "6": [[1, 80, 1250], [2, 1250, 3497], [3, 3497, 5097], [4, 5097, 7300]], "7": [[1, 210, 1904], [2, 1904, 3201], [3, 3201, 4207], [4, 4207, 5850]], "8": [[1, 180,